{"id":"n-20261019-zhmitm","category":"gaming","display_title":"Classic NES Games Worth Playing","display_title_he":"משחקי NES קלאסיים שכדאי לשחק בהם","short_summary":"A review of ten classic Nintendo Entertainment System games that remain engaging and worth playing from start to finish today.","english_level":"C1","words":460,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Polygon","domain":"polygon.com","url":"https://www.polygon.com/best-nes-games","title":"10 NES Games That Are Still Worth Playing From Start to Finish","published_at":"2026-10-19T02:34:47.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-19T02:34:47.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-19T06:28:27.036Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Back on October 18, 1985, Nintendo launched the Nintendo Entertainment System in North America with a modest lineup that included Super Mario Bros. and Excitebike. Within a few short years, the platform accumulated a vast library of hundreds of titles, effectively silencing skepticism about the video game industry's viability following early decade struggles. While many early software releases now feel like historical relics compared to modern generations, a select few timeless titles continue to warrant a complete playthrough from start to finish.","Leading the selection is Ninja Gaiden, celebrated for introducing the agile hero Ryu Hayabusa amid brutal difficulty spikes where aggressive bosses and even hostile birds can quickly defeat an unsuspecting player. The game inspired two sequels, and while Tecmo later revived the series with titles like 2005’s Ninja Gaiden Black on the original Xbox, the original remains the ultimate starting point. Another essential franchise entry is Castlevania 3: Dracula’s Curse, which perfected early series mechanics by offering multiple character choices and branching paths through gothic stages. Players still enjoy multiple runs through its challenging environments, testing new strategies and weapon combinations against the forces of darkness. Similarly, The Legend of Zelda established open-ended exploration after arriving in North America in 1987, allowing players to tackle labyrinths in flexible orders. By exploring hidden caves and gathering crucial equipment, players work to defeat Ganon and rescue Hyrule twice.","Role-playing fans find deep satisfaction in Dragon Warrior 4, which cleverly structures its narrative through distinct episodic heroes before uniting them in a sprawling final chapter. This technical mastery makes the final 8-bit installment remarkably memorable. Platforming enthusiasts can still enjoy Kirby’s Adventure, a colorful late-era title that highlights the pink character's signature ability to absorb enemy traits across Dream Land. For action seekers, Contra offers a famously concise, cooperative alien-shooting experience based on the arcade original, which becomes manageable through the legendary Konami code entered on the title screen. Meanwhile, Mega Man 2 is widely regarded as the most balanced and replayable entry among the franchise's initial six installments, avoiding the tedious filler and robot stages that burdened later sequels.","Sports and adventure rounding out the list provide equal renown. Mike Tyson’s Punch-Out!! pits the compact fighter Little Mac against a diverse global roster of unique personalities and attack patterns, culminating in an iconic bout that remains deeply etched in player memories. DuckTales rewards adventurous exploration across exotic environments ranging from the Amazon and the Himalayas to the Moon. This version is still accessible today as part of The Disney Afternoon Collection on modern consoles and PC. Finally, Super Mario Bros. 3 stands out through its vast assortment of creative worlds, imaginative power-ups, floating airships, and varied stage designs, cementing its status as a pinnacle of retro gaming excellence that players can experience directly from start to finish."],"facts":[{"fact":"On October 18, 1985, Nintendo released the Nintendo Entertainment System in North America alongside games like Super Mario Bros. and Excitebike.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Polygon published a list of 10 NES games that are still worth playing from start to finish.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The 10 recommended games include Ninja Gaiden, Castlevania 3: Dracula's Curse, The Legend of Zelda, Dragon Warrior 4, Kirby's Adventure, Contra, Mega Man 2, Mike Tyson's Punch-Out!!, DuckTales, and Super Mario Bros. 3.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Back","lemma":"back","pos":"adverb","he":"בחזרה","name":false},{"text":"on","lemma":"on","pos":"preposition","he":"ב-","name":false},{"text":"October","lemma":"October","pos":"proper noun","he":"אוקטובר","name":true},{"text":"18","lemma":"18","pos":"number","he":"18","name":false},{"text":"1985","lemma":"1985","pos":"number","he":"1985","name":false},{"text":"Nintendo","lemma":"Nintendo","pos":"proper noun","he":"נינטנדו","name":true},{"text":"launched","lemma":"launch","pos":"verb","he":"השיק","name":false},{"text":"the","lemma":"the","pos":"definite article","he":"ה-","name":false},{"text":"Nintendo Entertainment System","lemma":"Nintendo Entertainment System","pos":"proper noun","he":"נינטנדו אנטרטיינמנט סיסטם","name":true},{"text":"in","lemma":"in","pos":"preposition","he":"ב-","name":false},{"text":"North America","lemma":"North America","pos":"proper noun","he":"צפון אמריקה","name":true},{"text":"with","lemma":"with","pos":"preposition","he":"עם","name":false},{"text":"a","lemma":"a","pos":"indefinite article","he":"א","name":false},{"text":"modest","lemma":"modest","pos":"adjective","he":"ענוו","name":false},{"text":"lineup","lemma":"lineup","pos":"noun","he":"מערך","name":false},{"text":"that","lemma":"that","pos":"pronoun","he":"שה","name":false},{"text":"included","lemma":"include","pos":"verb","he":"כלל","name":false},{"text":"Super Mario Bros.","lemma":"Super Mario Bros.","pos":"prope